{"kappa":{"id":"72c21eb6-d459-4940-b677-2c401b7d21a5","word":"kappa","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"Greek letter","tags":["masculine"],"word":"capa"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"Greek letter","tags":["masculine"],"word":"cá"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"wikidata":["Q14401"],"senseid":["en:Q14401"],"glosses":["The tenth letter of the Greek alphabet."],"tags":["countable","uncountable"],"id":"c7647ccc-da9a-4224-b099-8dd7540e72fd"},{"topics":["business","finance"],"categories":["en:Finance"],"links":[["finance","finance#Noun"],["option","option"],["volatility","volatility"],["underlying","underlying"],["asset","asset"]],"raw_glosses":["(finance) A measurement of the sensitivity of the value of an option to changes in the implied volatility of the price of the underlying asset."],"glosses":["A measurement of the sensitivity of the value of an option to changes in the implied volatility of the price of the underlying asset."],"tags":["countable","uncountable"],"id":"e8449614-ecdf-4a43-a10f-e45af1933d8c"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[{"sense":"measure of derivative price sensitivity","word":"tau"},{"sense":"measure of derivative price sensitivity","word":"vega"}]},"kaput":{"id":"b71feab2-2117-4310-b4d7-c0f1e8922d02","word":"kaput","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"out of order","tags":["masculine"],"word":"enguiçado"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"out of order","tags":["masculine"],"word":"pifado"}],"pos":"adj","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"My car went kaput.","bold_text_offsets":[[12,17]],"type":"example","id":"135adf09-cdc3-4d73-9898-a4ec5e3c7454"},{"text":"His career is kaput.","bold_text_offsets":[[14,19]],"type":"example","id":"d41746ce-b466-487d-a6a6-70c1b8b60618"},{"text":"Her marriage went kaput.","bold_text_offsets":[[18,23]],"type":"example","id":"c12b8565-3000-49f4-8fd0-e722d35a7c46"},{"text":"German propaganda loudspeaker: […] The Statue of Liberty is KAPUT.\n Captain Miller: \"The Statue of Liberty is kaput\" – huh, that's disconcerting.","ref":"1998, Saving Private Ryan (motion picture):","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[60,65],[110,115]],"id":"3d98a62a-708c-4802-a216-8feaab81a3ed"},{"text":"In the book, his conclusion is simple: capitalism is kaput, celebrity charity won’t plug holes, revolution is the only solution. Yet it also feels like a bit of a cop-out: he insists all this can be achieved through love, peace and understanding.","ref":"2014 October 11, Simon Hattenstone, “Russell Brand: ‘I want to address the alienation and despair’”, in The Guardian, archived from the original on 01 Jul 2022:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[53,58]],"id":"aa79e21b-931e-44eb-b2b6-808c08321007"},{"text":"Many Trump voters, in other words, have had it. At this point, it seems safe to declare that the historic coalition that powered the president’s second reelection is finished—kaput.","ref":"2026 April 16, Yvonne Wingett Sanchez, Elaine Godfrey, “Trump Voters Are Over It”, in Jeffrey Goldberg, editor, The Atlantic, Washington, D.C.: The Atlantic Monthly Group, →ISSN, →OCLC:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[175,180]],"id":"f5bf098c-f4d4-48da-b8a7-5407ff44d13b"}],"categories":["English adjectives","English doublets","English entries with incorrect language header","English informal terms","English lemmas","English terms borrowed from German","English terms derived from French","English terms derived from German","English terms with homophones","English terms with quotations","English terms with usage examples","English uncomparable adjectives","Entries with translation boxes","Pages with 11 entries","Pages with entries","Rhymes:English/uːt","Rhymes:English/uːt/2 syllables","Rhymes:English/ʊt","Rhymes:English/ʊt/2 syllables","Terms with Afrikaans translations","Terms with Catalan translations","Terms with Danish translations","Terms with Dutch translations","T